=== ssh-copy-id ===
USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  ssh-copy-id [-h|-?|-f|-n|-s|-x] [-i [identity_file]] [-p port] [-F
      alternative ssh_config file] [-t target_path] [[-o <ssh -o options>]
      ...] [user@]hostname


FLAGS (9) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-f                              force mode -- copy keys without trying to
                                check if they are already installed
-n                              dry run -- no keys are actually copied
-s                              use sftp -- use sftp instead of executing
                                remote-commands. Can be useful if the remote
                                only allows sftp
-x                              debug -- enables -x in this shell, for
                                debugging
-h                              print this help
 or -?
-i [identity_file]
-p port
-F alternative ssh_config file
-t target_path
